# Keep the build context small and free of host-specific state.
#
# Docker matches these patterns against the whole path, and a leading `*` does
# NOT cross directory separators — `*.tsbuildinfo` matches only the repo root.
# Anything that can appear inside a workspace package needs an explicit `**/`
# form as well. Getting this wrong is not a size problem: a stale
# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo copied in while dist is excluded tells `tsc --build`
# everything is already compiled, so it emits nothing and the build fails much
# later with confusing "cannot find module" errors.

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist
dist-types
**/dist-types
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# node_modules in particular must never be copied: the image resolves its own
# for linux, and a Windows tree would carry the wrong native binaries.

.git
.github
.data

.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

.output
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
app/Client/e2e

docs
*.md
!README.md

.vscode
.idea
.claude
.claude.json
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile.debug
